PS(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    ps - show the process table

SYNOPSIS
    ps

DESCRIPTION
    Prints aligned PID, PPID, PGID, USER, STATE, TIME, RSS and NAME columns
    from /dev/proc. The kernel supplies the snapshot, its accounting units
    and the effective uid of each process, which ps shows as the account
    name of /etc/passwd, or as the number when no account has it.

SEE ALSO
    id(1), sh(1), man(1), index(7)
